.TH PACMAN 6.SH NAMEpacman \- Pac-Man in a character maze.SH SYNOPSIS\fBpacman\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONYou are\fBOS9\fRin a maze of dots, chased by ghosts named CPM, MPM, RAM and ROM.  It asks your name and whether you want instructions, thendraws the maze.  The keypad moves you:\fB8\fR up, \fB2\fR down, \fB4\fR left, \fB6\fR right;\fR\fBq\fRquits..PPBefore it draws it runs OS-9's\fBtmode\fRto set the terminal\fBnopause noecho\fR,\fRso\fBtmode\fRfrom your own system has to be on the execution path.  It positions thecursor with ESC = followed by the row and column plus 32 each, theADM-3A and TeleVideo sequence, and the maze paints only on a terminalthat understands it..SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/pacman/board\fR.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/pacman/board.2\fRthe mazes..TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/pacman/Document\fRthe instructions it offers..TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/pacman/score\fRthe high scores..SH SEE ALSOsnake, rogue